{"name":"Disruption with GitHub services","status":"resolved","created_at":"2026-10-30T14:31:16.537Z","updated_at":"2026-11-18T21:49:12.661Z","monitoring_at":"2026-10-30T14:49:46.388Z","resolved_at":"2026-10-30T15:02:51.002Z","impact":"critical","shortlink":"https://stspg.io/6p81rf34z4nc","scheduled_for":null,"scheduled_until":null,"scheduled_remind_prior":false,"scheduled_reminded_at":null,"impact_override":"critical","scheduled_auto_in_progress":false,"scheduled_auto_completed":false,"metadata":{},"started_at":"2026-10-30T14:31:16.529Z","reminder_intervals":null,"id":"nxy2l0ssxm10","page_id":"kctbh9vrtdwd","incident_updates":[{"status":"resolved","body":"On October 30, 2026, between 14:20 and 14:29 UTC, customers experienced errors across multiple GitHub services. Affected services include Git operations, GraphQL and REST API, Pull Requests, and Issues. At peak, about 3.5% of API requests failed. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThe incident was caused by slow database requests that held connections open longer than expected, which used all available connections to one of our primary databases. Service recovered at 14:29 UTC once connections were released. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eSince the incident, we have fixed the code path that held connections open and increased the processing capacity of our database connection layer. We are also improving alerting for this type of overload.","created_at":"2026-10-30T15:02:51.002Z","wants_twitter_update":false,"twitter_updated_at":null,"updated_at":"2026-11-18T21:49:12.655Z","display_at":"2026-10-30T15:02:51.002Z","deliver_notifications":true,"tweet_id":null,"id":"kw3pxydwdqj4","incident_id":"nxy2l0ssxm10","custom_tweet":null,"affected_components":[{"code":"kr09ddfgbfsf","name":"Issues","old_status":"operational","new_status":"operational"},{"code":"vg70hn9s2tyj","name":"Pages","old_status":"operational","new_status":"operational"}]},{"status":"monitoring","body":"The degradation affecting Pages has been mitigated. We